                <pb facs="0852" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.822/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-09T10:00:00-00:44">July 9, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 9—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Your 27, July 7, 10 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">6 p.m.</hi>] Liberian
                    Government agreeable to engrossing final text with all changes as referred to by
                    the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
                <pb facs="0853" n="845" xml:id="pg845"/>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For text of treaty signed August 8, 1938, see Department of State Treaty
                        Series No. 956, or 54 Stat, 1739.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
